# Upgrade-Safe Only — Standing Constraint

Every customization for MY School must stay inside the `myschools` app, use Frappe's public/fixture primitives, and survive a `bench update` without manual intervention.

## Why

Ali deliberately chose open-source Frappe to inherit upstream maintenance (security patches, browser compat, performance work, new doctypes). Any change that forks core, monkey-patches internals, or stands up a parallel frontend defeats that choice — it converts free upstream work into permanent local maintenance debt.

He stated this explicitly:

> "We don't need custom app which requires maintenance effort... we must stay in safer position where customisations won't stop/break/hard to upgrade to Frappe's newer versions."

## How to apply

When scoping any feature or recommendation, only propose options from the **Safe** list. If the only way to deliver something is from the **Banned** list, surface that constraint to Ali before designing — don't quietly compromise.

### Safe (use freely)

- Custom Fields & Property Setters (fixture-exported via Customize Form)
- DocTypes in our own app (`myschools/my_school_erp/doctype/`)
- `hooks.py` keys: `doc_events`, `scheduler_events`, `permission_query_conditions`, `override_doctype_class` (sparingly), `app_include_css`, `web_include_css`, `role_home_page`, `fixtures`
- Workspace / Module Profile / Workflow / Print Format / Notification / Email Template / Letter Head / Dashboard / Number Card **fixtures**
- Per-doctype JS (`mys_branch.js`, `mys_branch_list.js`) using documented `frappe.ui.form.on()` / `frappe.listview_settings` APIs
- Custom Pages (`bench new-page`) for dashboard-style screens
- **Web Forms + `www/` Jinja templates** for portal flows (this is Frappe's native portal — use it instead of a custom SPA)
- Server Scripts / Client Scripts (exportable as fixtures)
- CSS overrides via `app_include_css` that target Frappe's CSS variables (`--primary`, `--text-color`, etc.) — NOT internal class selectors

### Banned

- Editing files inside `apps/frappe/` or `apps/erpnext/`
- Monkey-patching Frappe/ERPNext modules at runtime
- Forking ERPNext or Frappe Education to modify core
- Selecting undocumented internal Frappe DOM classes in custom JS (those change between versions)
- Separate SPA frontends (Vue/React/Next) that talk to Frappe over REST as a parallel codebase — use Frappe Web Forms + `www/` instead
- Hardcoding behavior already provided by a Frappe hook or fixture

## Plan implication

**Phase 7 of the roadmap is NOT a custom SPA.** It is Frappe Web Forms + `www/` Jinja templates inside the `myschools` app.

